// A subexpression can be annotated with a type, `(e: T)` -- or, as a call
// argument, `f(e: T)` without the extra parens. This disambiguates an
// otherwise-underdetermined expression like the empty set literal `{||}`,
// whose element type would otherwise be unresolvable when passed to an
// uninstantiated generic functor.
val s = Library.DisjSet.set({||} : Set[Int])

val t = (1 + 1 : Int)
